Proofs that we made from proofs that Anthropic licensed under the Apache License
2.0 or the MIT licence, at the recipient's option, keep those licences and their
file headers. The licence texts are LICENSES/anthropic-proofs-LICENSE (Apache
License 2.0) and LICENSES/anthropic-proofs-LICENSE-MIT (MIT), and the notices
that came with the proofs are LICENSES/anthropic-proofs-NOTICE; the build record
of each such proof names these three files.

Files under projects/*/*/source/ are copies of fuzz targets exactly as they were
built. Each copy keeps its upstream licence, which its harness.yaml names, or
gives as NOASSERTION where it is not recorded yet. Where a harness has no
source/ directory, the files it was built from are in the project's recipe
archive (one of those that release.yaml lists under recipes) or in the
project's source archive.

The source archives attached to a release (<project>-src.tar.zst,
toolchain-src.tar.zst, sysroot-src.tar.zst) hold upstream source trees, each
under its own licence.

The binaries attached to a release are combined works under the licences of
everything linked into them: the library, the harness, the C library (musl, MIT),
the compiler's runtime libraries (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception), the
static-asan patches to the sanitizer runtime and to musl (MIT), this
repository's driver (MIT), and any other library they link. Each project's
binary archive carries the licence files of every component compiled into its
binaries, verbatim, under LICENSES/<component>/. No harness.yaml records the
combined licence of its binaries yet; the build record of each proof lists the
components and their licences. A binary under a GPL or LGPL licence is attached
only together with its complete corresponding source.

